From: Nicolin Chen <nicolinc@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2025 23:35:17 -0700
Subject: iommufd: Return EOPNOTSUPP for failures due to driver bugs
Patch-mainline: v6.17-rc1
Git-commit: 0c6e0ae7a7e49fb0e781d3fbf24004e1b6b586d1
References: jsc#PED-16989

It's more accurate to report EOPNOTSUPP when an ioctl failed due to driver
bug, since there is nothing wrong with the user space side.

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/r/623bb6f0e8fdd7b9c5745a2f99f280163f9f1f5a.1749882255.git.nicolinc@nvidia.com
Signed-off-by: Nicolin Chen <nicolinc@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Kevin Tian <kevin.tian@intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Lu Baolu <baolu.lu@linux.intel.com>
Reviewed-by: Pranjal Shrivastava <praan@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carlos López <clopez@suse.de>
---
 drivers/iommu/iommufd/device.c       |    2 +-
 drivers/iommu/iommufd/hw_pagetable.c |    4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/iommu/iommufd/device.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/iommufd/device.c
@@ -1321,7 +1321,7 @@ int iommufd_get_hw_info(struct iommufd_u
 		 */
 		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(cmd->out_data_type ==
 				 IOMMU_HW_INFO_TYPE_NONE)) {
-			rc = -ENODEV;
+			rc = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 			goto out_free;
 		}
 	} else {
--- a/drivers/iommu/iommufd/hw_pagetable.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/iommufd/hw_pagetable.c
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@ iommufd_hwpt_nested_alloc(struct iommufd
 	iommu_domain_set_sw_msi(hwpt->domain, iommufd_sw_msi);
 
 	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(hwpt->domain->type != IOMMU_DOMAIN_NESTED)) {
-		rc = -EINVAL;
+		rc = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		goto out_abort;
 	}
 	return hwpt_nested;
@@ -307,7 +307,7 @@ iommufd_viommu_alloc_hwpt_nested(struct
 	iommu_domain_set_sw_msi(hwpt->domain, iommufd_sw_msi);
 
 	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(hwpt->domain->type != IOMMU_DOMAIN_NESTED)) {
-		rc = -EINVAL;
+		rc = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		goto out_abort;
 	}
 	return hwpt_nested;
